      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## FLUX 3 multi-reference, prepared\n\nThree references normalised to a sensible size, checked in order on a contact strip, then sent to FLUX 3 Image together \u2014 so nothing is rejected for size and nothing arrives in the wrong slot.\n\n**Scale Image to Total Pixels** (core) brings each reference to **1.0 MP** with lanczos. The API refuses a reference over 16 MP and one under 256 \u00d7 256, and a phone photo uploaded at full size just makes the call slower. Raise `megapixels` for image 1 if the output should keep more of its detail \u2014 its frame sets the output's.\n\n**Stitch Images** (core) lays the three out left to right in socket order, labelled nothing but order itself: the leftmost is *image 1*. Check it before you spend \u2014 the prompt refers to the references by number, so a swapped Load Image is a different request.\n\n**Image Comparer** sets the room (image 1) against the result.\n\nConnect more references and more sockets appear on the FLUX 3 node, up to 10; extend the stitch chain to match.\n\n### Needs\n[rgthree-comfy](https://github.com/rgthree/rgthree-comfy). **Manager \u2192 Install Missing Custom Nodes** finds it if the graph loads with red nodes.\n\n## The prompt lives in one node\n\nThe **Shared Prompt** node feeds every FLUX 3 `prompt` in this graph, so there is one\nplace to edit it. It emits a plain string, **not** a list, so each node it feeds still runs once."
      ],
      "title": "Read me",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
